INSERT [dbo].[PageTranslations] ([Id], [PageId], [Title], [Summary], [Body], [SeoTitle], [SeoDescription], [Language], [Sections]) VALUES (N'019fa37a-8e56-77a8-a664-b6b02f3fd1af', N'019fa37a-8e56-75b1-9712-99e8447eefa2', N'Intellectual Property Rights', N'The Saudi Water Authority provides comprehensive terms of use, privacy policies, and Intellectual Property Rights protections to ensure user trust and compliance with global standards. As sustainability is one of our core values, we follow an ambitious roadmap aligned with the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia’s Vision 2030, ensuring transparency and security in every aspect of our operations. Intellectual Property Rights', N'All content available on the Saudi Water Authority''s website, including texts, images, graphics, designs, and logos, are the property of the Authority and are protected under local and international intellectual property laws. The reproduction, distribution, or modification of any of these contents without prior written consent from the Authority is prohibited. Unauthorized use may result in legal action against violators.
Trademarks
The trademarks and logos used by the Saudi Water Authority are the property of the Authority and may not be used in any way without prior written permission. Any unauthorized use of the Authority''s trademarks, whether for commercial or non-commercial purposes, constitutes an intellectual property violation and will be addressed legally.
Licensing and Fair Use
The Saudi Water Authority may permit the use of some content available on its website for non-commercial purposes, provided prior written permission is obtained and the fair use policy is adhered to. Such use should be for educational or research purposes and should not infringe on the Authority''s Intellectual Property Rights or cause any financial harm.
Intellectual Property Violations
In the event of any Intellectual Property Rights violations concerning the Saudi Water Authority, the Authority will take all necessary legal actions to protect its rights. Users are encouraged to report any potential violations as soon as they are discovered, and the matter will be investigated with appropriate measures taken. The Authority reserves its full right to seek compensation for any damages resulting from such violations.', N'Intellectual Property Rights', N'The Saudi Water Authority provides comprehensive terms of use, privacy policies, and Intellectual Property Rights protections to ensure user trust and compliance with global standards. As sustainability is one of our core values, we follow an ambitious roadmap aligned with the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia’s Vision 2030, ensuring transparency and security in every aspect of our operations. Intellectual Property Rights', 'en', NULL)
GO
INSERT [dbo].[PageTranslations] ([Id], [PageId], [Title], [Summary], [Body], [SeoTitle], [SeoDescription], [Language], [Sections]) VALUES (N'019fa37a-8e57-7314-b41b-b6bbf3b8aad5', N'019fa37a-8e57-75fb-91d5-8bfba36d9a81', N'Saudi Irrigation Organization​', N'The Saudi Irrigation Organization is a public governmental institution established by the Council of Ministers’ Resolution No. (542) dated 26/08/1438 AH, suc...', N'Saudi Irrigation Organization​
The Saudi Irrigation Organization is a public governmental institution established by the Council of Ministers’ Resolution No. (542) dated 26/08/1438 AH, succeeding the Irrigation and Drainage Authority in Al-Ahsa, which was founded in 1392 AH to manage irrigation and drainage operations in the region. The organization enjoys legal personality and administrative and financial independence. It operates under the close affiliation of the Ministry of Environment, Water and Agriculture and is responsible for managing, operating, and developing irrigation activities across the Kingdom. All responsibilities and tasks related to irrigation have been transferred to the organization, which is diligently working to achieve its strategic objectives and advance the irrigation sector, reclaimed water use, and dam management in Saudi Arabia. The organization adopts an ambitious vision aimed at ensuring the sustainability of water resources, improving usage efficiency, and preserving natural resources. This aligns with efforts to promote the use of non-conventional water sources, maximize the benefits of dam water, and expand their use to meet the needs of agricultural, industrial, and urban sectors. The organization is also working to develop water infrastructure and enhance its quality, with a strong focus on innovation, the adoption of modern irrigation systems, continuous improvement, and boosting overall effectiveness and efficiency.
Roles
Enhancing the sustainability of water resources by operating and managing dams and water networks, while securing reliable water supply for the agricultural, industrial, and urban sectors.
Continuously improving water quality and network coverage across all regions of the Kingdom, and ensuring compliance with both local and international standards.
Providing training initiatives to support the sustainable production in small-scale farms.
Contributing to economic development through infrastructure enhancement of water transmission and distribution networks and dams.
Raising awareness among consumers about the beneficial uses of surface water, renewable water, and other water resources.
Establishing strict safety standards for the management of dams and water transmission and distribution networks, and developing dam management strategies.
Vision
Excellence in managing and developing the irrigation, water reuse, and dam sectors to achieve sustainability.
Mission
Expanding the use of sustainable water resources by developing an integrated network for water transmission and distribution, utilizing advanced technologies to enhance field efficiency and ensure a safe and continuous water supply for all sectors.
Values
Responsibility
Efficiency
Customer focus
Professionalism
Sustainability
Objectives
Resource sustainability
Service quality and availability
Social well-being
Economic contribution
Awareness
Safety
Explore Our Website', N'Saudi Irrigation Organization​', N'The Saudi Irrigation Organization is a public governmental institution established by the Council of Ministers’ Resolution No. (542) dated 26/08/1438 AH, suc...', 'en', NULL)
