INSERT [dbo].[PageTranslations] ([Id], [PageId], [Title], [Summary], [Body], [SeoTitle], [SeoDescription], [Language], [Sections]) VALUES (N'019fa37a-8e57-7fb2-8314-cd55cc443344', N'019fa37a-8e57-7d00-9f4b-66d9302a4396', N'Open Data Polic', N'The Saudi Water Authority provides open data for all portal users to enhance public awareness, promote engagement, and support informed access to services. The available datasets are non-commercial and educational, published transparently in alignment with Vision 2030.', N'What is Open Data?
Open data refers to the concept that certain data should be made freely accessible to all visitors and users of the Authority’s portal. This allows them to use and republish the data without restrictions. The purpose of open data is to promote participation and enhance public knowledge. Visitors and users are encouraged to review the data usage policy published on the portal to stay informed about updates and conditions. All open data made available by the Ministry’s portal is intended for awareness and non-commercial use.
Users of Open Data
All users of the Authority’s portal are entitled to access open data. They are also allowed to use and reuse the data at their own discretion and responsibility, with access guaranteed for all.
Responsibility of Data Users
Users of open data are responsible for any reuse of data provided through the Authority’s portal. They must ensure that such reuse does not result in errors or misrepresentations regarding the content, origin, or history of the data.
Authority Disclaimer
The Saudi Water Authority shall not be held liable for any damage or misuse that may occur to bodies as a result of using the published open data. The Authority does not guarantee the continuity and availability of the data, whether in whole or in part. Furthermore, the Authority assumes no responsibility for any loss or harm that users may encounter due to the reuse of this data.
Terms of Reuse
The user must not distort the data or its source.
This data must not be used for political purposes, to support illegal activities or criminal behavior, or to promote discrimination, racism, or actions that incite cultural or societal discord, and it must not be used in any way that conflicts with the laws, customs, or values of the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia.
Reused data must be properly attributed by including a link to the Saudi Water Authority’s portal, ensuring the preservation of data integrity, credibility, and intellectual property.
The Open Data Policy is formulated in accordance with the National Data Governance Policies issued by the Saudi Authority for Data and Artificial Intelligence (SADAIA). For further information about the regulations, general rules for open data and the right to access information, please
Click here', N'Open Data Polic', N'The Saudi Water Authority provides open data for all portal users to enhance public awareness, promote engagement, and support informed access to services. The available datasets are non-commercial and educational, published transparently in alignment with Vision 2030.', 'en', NULL)
GO
INSERT [dbo].[PageTranslations] ([Id], [PageId], [Title], [Summary], [Body], [SeoTitle], [SeoDescription], [Language], [Sections]) VALUES (N'019fa37a-8e55-7d7d-a015-d47d83708f7f', N'019fa37a-8e55-743b-bd2f-f022a5954a3b', N'قنوات التواصل', N'تهدف هذه الصفحة إلى استقبال الاستفسارات العامة المتعلقة بالهيئة السعودية للمياه، بالإضافة إلى المقترحات التطويرية، وأي ملاحظات أو صعوبات تقنية تواجه الزائر أثناء تصفح الموقع الالكتروني​', N'تهدف هذه الصفحة إلى استقبال الاستفسارات العامة المتعلقة بالهيئة السعودية للمياه، بالإضافة إلى المقترحات التطويرية، وأي ملاحظات أو صعوبات تقنية تواجه الزائر أثناء تصفح الموقع الالكتروني​
